{
  "name": "POC1 — Builder-return pipeline (Release 1, Business partition only)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "path": "poc1-builder-return",
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "responseMode": "onReceived"
      },
      "id": "builder-return-webhook",
      "name": "Builder Return Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "INBOUND. A Builder return artifact (zip + manifest) arrives. Business partition only (05_ §2). EXTERNAL-UNTRUSTED until the envelope node. 09_ §2: this is the Release-1 workload, not the Release-2 call flow.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// 09_ §2 R1P-04 — the identity tuple, all five components. A raw archive\n// hash alone is NOT identity: two tasks may legitimately submit byte-\n// identical artifacts, and one task may resubmit with changed routing.\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\nreturn items.map(i => {\n  const b64 = i.json.artifact_b64 || '';\n  const digest = crypto.createHash('sha256')\n                       .update(Buffer.from(b64, 'base64')).digest('hex');\n  return { json: {\n    envelope: { trust: 'external-untrusted', partition: 'business',\n                source: 'builder-relay', received_at: new Date().toISOString() },\n    // the five components (C-1)\n    task_id: i.json.task_id,\n    transition: i.json.transition,          // e.g. 'builder->fable'\n    artifact_digest: digest,                // computed here, not trusted\n    target_role: i.json.target_role,        // SYMBOLIC role (C-2)\n    submission_epoch: Number(i.json.submission_epoch ?? 1),\n    // R1P-05: artifact-handling measurements the session records\n    artifact_bytes: Buffer.from(b64, 'base64').length,\n    manifest_file_count: (i.json.manifest_files || []).length,\n    content_forwarded: Boolean(b64)\n  } };\n});"
      },
      "id": "apply-envelope-and-bind-identity",
      "name": "Apply Envelope and Bind Identity",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "BOUNDARY + C-1. The digest is COMPUTED from the artifact here rather than taken from the sender. `target_role` is symbolic; the wrapper resolves it.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc1/review-case",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "ai-os---open-review-case",
      "name": "AI OS — Open Review Case",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "AUTHORITY. Returns either a resume token (new case) or a duplicate-suppression result carrying the PRIOR receipt — R1P-04 test (1). An unauthorized target_role is REJECTED here, distinguishably — test (3).",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "string": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.outcome }}",
              "operation": "equals",
              "value2": "case-opened"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "duplicate-or-rejected?",
      "name": "Duplicate or Rejected?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "R1P-04 (1) and (3) are OBSERVED here: duplicate-suppressed and rejected-unauthorized-target take the false branch and are recorded as distinct outcomes, never as a success.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resume": "webhook"
      },
      "id": "wait-for-owner-decision",
      "name": "Wait for Owner Decision",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "TRANSPORT ONLY. The provider carries the pause; the decision is made on the AI OS/Discord card. The provider never learns the case id.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.AIOS_WRAPPER_BASE }}/poc1/verify-decision",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({token: $('AI OS — Open Review Case').item.json.resume_token}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "X-Provider-Key",
              "value": "={{ $env.AIOS_PROVIDER_KEY }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "verify-decision-token",
      "name": "Verify Decision Token",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "AUTHORITY. ONLY the token — the endpoint is an allowlist and refuses any other field. Returns the ActionRequest plus a single-use execution capability, or pending, or a refusal.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "boolean": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.authorized }}",
              "value2": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "authorized?",
      "name": "Authorized?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "GATE. No capability, no relay.",
      "notesInFlow": false
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.action_request.endpoint }}",
        "method": "POST",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({capability: $json.execution_capability, action_request_id: $json.action_request.id, case_id: $json.action_request.case_id, payload: $json.action_request.payload}) }}",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "specifyHeaders": "keypair",
        "headerParameters": {
